      "problem": "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=\\{-2,2\\}\\times \\{-1,0,1\\}$ in the Cartesian plane?",
      "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, computing $\\{-2,2\\}\\times \\{-1,0,1\\}$ gives the following set:\n\n$$\nS=\\{(-2,-1),(-2,0),(-2,1),(2,-1),(2,0),(2,1)\\}.\n$$\n\nOur visualization of this set is shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14242415/assets/5dd3ff71d17188adaa68632b6d16aed1f41e1975ec4ddd321a8160fabb0e16b8.png)",
